https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Y7lmAc3LKWM  (Capo 2)

Along with Gordon Lightfoot's "Pony Man" this is one of the great children’s songs.  The next to last stanza is played softly denoting Puff’s sadness, while the final stanza is played up-tempo in recognition that Puff still lives and awaits the next child to love. 

TIP:  If transposing, play the root chord of the (CaddG) and (Gadd) and add the 5th note as needed.

TIP:  (C), (G), and (D) can be played instead of (CaddG), (Gadd) and (Bm) if you'd rather.


